WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:02.190
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar

00:00:02.649 --> 00:00:06.269
Today MIT ranks as one of the top universities in the world.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:12.420
Nearly 150 years ago, this question appeared on its admissions exam.

00:00:13.719 --> 00:00:18.419
"The perpendicular dropped from the vertex of the right angle upon the hypotenuse

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.529
divides it into two segments of 9 and 16 feet respectively.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:27.599
Find the lengths of the perpendicular, and the two legs of the triangle."

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:33.360
Give this problem a try. And when you're ready, keep watching the video for the solution.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:41.969
We'll get started by drawing a diagram. We have a right triangle.

00:00:43.629 --> 00:00:49.139
We're going to draw a perpendicular from the vertex of the right angle to the hypotenuse.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:55.349
This divides the hypotenuse into two segments of 9 and 16 feet.

00:00:56.559 --> 00:01:00.929
We need to find the lengths of the perpendicular and the two legs of the triangle.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:08.879
The perpendicular to the hypotenuse of a right triangle creates a special set of triangles.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.849
The green triangle here and the blue triangle here are similar triangles.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:20.669
This means the ratio of their lengths and angles are the same.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:29.909
In particular, the length of the shorter leg of the green triangle to its longer leg will be the same ratio as the

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.900
length of the shorter leg of the blue triangle to its longer leg.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:40.440
So we can set the ratio of the shorter leg to the longer leg of each triangle equal to each other.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:48.300
In the green triangle, we have 9 divided by p. And in the blue triangle we have p divided by 16

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:57.680
We can cross multiply these fractions to get p-squared is equal to 9 times 16 which equals 144

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:03.920
This means p is equal to the positive square root of 144 which is 12

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:11.160
So we've solved for one part of the problem that the perpendicular has the length of 12

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:15.519
We now need to solve for the two legs of the triangle

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:23.140
Notice that each leg of a triangle is equal to the hypotenuse of one of these smaller triangles

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.640
We could use the Pythagorean theorem to figure out the legs

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.140
In the green triangle,

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:37.599
the length of the hypotenuse would be the square root of the sum of the squares of the legs of the green triangle.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.269
And the same thing is true in the blue triangle

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.310
But we don't need to go through these calculations if we notice one more thing.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:52.449
In each of these triangles the ratio of the shorter leg to the longer leg is 3:4

00:02:53.450 --> 00:03:00.339
So each of these smaller triangles is a scaled up version of the 3 4 5 right triangle

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:04.629
So we can solve for the hypotenuse by scaling appropriately

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:11.259
The green triangle has lengths which are three times that of a 3 4 5 right triangle

00:03:11.599 --> 00:03:16.059
Which means its hypotenuse has to be 3 times 5 which is 15

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.869
Similarly the blue triangle is

00:03:20.449 --> 00:03:23.949
scaled up 4 times a 3 4 5 right triangle

00:03:24.379 --> 00:03:28.569
so its hypotenuse will be 4 times 5 which is equal to 20.

00:03:29.269 --> 00:03:31.269
And that's the solution

00:03:31.669 --> 00:03:33.669
Did you figure it out?

